  "summary_en": "Grunge Rust procedurally generates a rust-like texture by stacking several noise layers. Its Rust controls set how much of the surface is fully rusted, bare, or partly rusted, so it can serve as a mask for rust damage.",
  "inputs": [
    "size_ref: representative layer that sets the output size and metadata"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Range: Amplitude scales values before Center; Center offsets them; Mask Contrast increases extremes",
    "Pattern: Element Size, Element Scale (with Per-Component Controls), Offset, Tile Size in image coordinates",
    "Coverage: balance of fully rusted (white) and unrusted (black) areas",
    "Softness: how much partial rust shows under the fully rusted areas",
    "Rust: how much partial rust shows under the unrusted areas",
    "Rust Size: flake size; higher values give larger flakes",
    "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Output can be negative or above 1 because layers store such values; use Clamp Minimum and Clamp Maximum",
    "Complement assumes values from 0 to 1",
    "The Contrast post-processing option differs from Noise Contrast on some noise nodes"
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Grunge Rust génère une texture de rouille par empilement de bruits, avec des réglages de couverture, de douceur et de taille de paillettes."
